<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n62168" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λάω</span></b>  (B) <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ᾰ]</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>seize, hold</i>,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κύων ἔχε ποικίλον ἐλλόν,
				ἀσπαίροντα λάων</span>
			<i>gripping</i> it as it struggled, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				19.229
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ μὲν λάε νεβρὸν ἀπάγχων</span>
			<i>gripped</i> the fawn as he was throttling it, ib.<i><span class="en">
				230
			</span></i>.—Also expld. by <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπολαυστικῶς ἔχων</span> (<i><span class="en">
				Aristarch.
			</span></i>) or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπολαυστικῶς ἐσθίων</span>
			(Sch., <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
			
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λάων</span>
			, who refers it alternatively to <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λάω</span> (A), but also has <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λάε:
				ἐψόφησεν, οἱ δὲ ἐφθέγγετο</span>; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λαήμεναι: φθέγγεσθαι</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Cyr.
			</span></i>).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
